\documentclass{article}
\title{Carbonate Ion Availability Under Ocean Acidification}
\author{J. Whitaker and M. Solis}
\date{April 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Speciation}
Dissolved inorganic carbon partitions between three dominant species in seawater.
We write $c = \(a + b\)$ for the combined concentration of the two charged ions,
where each term follows from the measured pH and the total alkalinity.
The remaining neutral fraction is set by the dissociation constants of carbonic acid.
\end{document}

